After running fit_loft_drag_time, use the optimized multiplier history from out(k) to replay that trajectory.

k = 1;  % Select the loft case to test
% Load optimized drag multiplier history
drag_study_scale('set', out(k).knots, out(k).knotScale);
% Run propagator
[R,V,time] = propagate_traj( ...
    runs(k).R(1,:), runs(k).V(1,:), ...
    runs(k).time(1), runs(k).time(end), dt);
% Reset drag multiplier to 1
drag_study_scale('reset');

Your existing Drag.m automatically applies the time-varying multiplier through:

inverseBeta = drag_study_scale(t) * model.K_norm * CD;

Important: Use out(k).knots and out(k).knotScale rather than out(k).scale, since those are the optimized control points used during fitting.

The resulting R, V, and time are your corrected trajectory, which you can compare directly against the corresponding truth trajectory.
